From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:50:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Kernel] K8V4 decode: FP16 exact dequant, split-half nibble
 packing, multi-page tiles

E2M1 codes shifted into FP16 bits are value * 2^-14, so V dequantizes with
two integer ops and one FP16 multiply (exact for every E2M1 x E4M3 product);
both GEMMs run in FP16 with FP32 accumulation. Byte j of a V row packs
elements j and j + D/2, so the PV GEMM splits into two halves without an
interleave. BLOCK_N may span several pages (per-row block ids).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/v1/attention/ops/k8v4_kv.py | 202 +++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 111 insertions(+), 91 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/attention/ops/k8v4_kv.py b/vllm/v1/attention/ops/k8v4_kv.py
index f198b0f03..55f55594a 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/attention/ops/k8v4_kv.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/attention/ops/k8v4_kv.py
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ split into three planes (the layout must keep each page's [H, N, C] bytes
 contiguous, i.e. an HND layout):
 
     [ K   : H x P x D      fp8 e4m3 ]
-    [ V   : H x P x D/2    uint8, two E2M1 codes per byte, low nibble first ]
+    [ V   : H x P x D/2    uint8, byte j = code[j] | code[j + D/2] << 4 ]
     [ Vsf : H x P x D/16   fp8 e4m3 block scales ]
 
 Numerics reproduce the QW38 accuracy emulation (FP8 keys, NVFP4 values):
@@ -22,7 +22,11 @@ keys `fp8(clamp(k / k_scale, +-448))`; values per 16 elements of `x / g`:
 E2M1 rounding `|y| < 2: rint(2|y|)/2; < 4: rint(|y|); < 5: 4; else 6`
 (half-even, and 5.0 rounds up to 6 as in the emulation), dequant
 `bf16((e2m1 * bs) * g)`. Dequantized values are exact in BF16 (<= 6
-significant bits) when g == 1.
+significant bits) when g == 1. The decode kernel dequantizes in FP16, which
+is exact for every E2M1 x E4M3 product (an E2M1 code shifted into FP16 bits is
+the value times 2^-14; the 2^14 is applied to the FP32 accumulator), and runs
+both GEMMs in FP16 with FP32 accumulation (BF16 Q converts exactly for
+|q| >= 2^-14); the global scale g multiplies the output.
 
 Kernels (Triton, no csrc):
   * `k8v4_store`: reshape_and_cache writer (slot mapping).
